    "type": "question",
    "label": "74",
    "prompt": "Solve $\\ln(x+7)+\\ln(x+2)=\\ln(x+5)+\\ln(x-2)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No solution.\n\nThe original domain is $x>2$, but combining the logarithms gives $x=-4$.",
      "worked": "All four logarithm arguments must be positive: $x>-7$, $x>-2$, $x>-5$ and $x>2$. Hence the original domain is $x>2$.\n\nUsing the addition property and equating the positive arguments:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln\\bigl((x+7)(x+2)\\bigr)&=\\ln\\bigl((x+5)(x-2)\\bigr)\\\\(x+7)(x+2)&=(x+5)(x-2)\\\\x^2+9x+14&=x^2+3x-10\\\\6x&=-24\\\\x&=-4\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-4$ does not satisfy $x>2$, there is no solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
